\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold the Saviour of mankind
\par Nailed to the shameful tree!
\par How vast the love that Him inclined
\par To bleed and die for thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Hark! how He groans! while nature shakes,
\par And earth's strong pillars bend;
\par The temple's veil in sunder breaks,
\par The solid marbles rend.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. 'Tis done! the precious ransom's paid;
\par Receive My soul! He cries:
\par See where He bows His sacred head!
\par He bows His head, and dies!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. But soon He'll break death's envious chain,
\par And in full glory shine:
\par O Lamb of God, was ever pain,
\par Was ever love, like Thine?\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

